node.doctext:
In [doc://perlsecret] - perl secret operators, there's 
<blockquote>
<c>
# remove empty array refs
@arrays = ( [], [1], [ 1, 2 ], [], [ 5 .. 9 ] );

# @filled = ( [1], [ 1, 2 ], [ 5 .. 9 ] );
@filled = grep +()= @$_, @arrays;
</c>
</blockquote>
with a note of:
<blockquote>
<b>(The + is in the above line is a no-op, used to tell grep that the parentheses are not enclosing its arguments.)</b>
</blockquote>

what does that note actually mean?
